sers/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01GzzMaECqLDUm3MRPYr5Qy3', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Request Cleanup System Fix - Requirements\\n\\n## Overview\\nFix the incomplete request cleanup system in ActivityTracker causing memory growth issues over long sessions.\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\nThe current ActivityTracker implementation has critical issues:\\n1. `clear_request()` method is incomplete - only has placeholder comment \\"For now, we\'ll keep the data\\"\\n2. Request-based activity filtering is not properly implemented in `get_agent_hierarchy()`\\n3. Activities accumulate indefinitely without cleanup mechanism\\n4. Memory usage grows unbounded during long sessions\\n5. No configurable retention policy for old activities\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Complete the `clear_request()` implementation to fully remove request data\\n2. Implement proper request-based activity filtering throughout the system\\n3. Add automatic cleanup mechanism for old activities with configurable retention\\n4. Ensure no data loss for active/recent requests\\n5. Maintain memory usage stability over long sessions\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- Complete `clear_request()` method implementation in ActivityTracker\\n- Fix request-based filtering in `get_agent_hierarchy()` and related methods\\n- Implement automatic cleanup with configurable retention (default 24 hours for completed requests)\\n- Add cleanup mechanism for old activities (configurable, default keep 10,000 most recent)\\n- Write comprehensive tests for all cleanup functionality\\n- Ensure thread safety for cleanup operations\\n- Add logging for cleanup operations\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Changes to activity data structure or API\\n- UI modifications (cleanup is backend-only)\\n- Database persistence changes\\n- WebSocket notification changes\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n### Functional Requirements\\n\\n#### R1: Complete Request Cleanup\\n- `clear_request(request_id)` must fully remove all data associated with a request:\\n  - All activities with matching `request_id`\\n  - Agent hierarchy entries for request agents\\n  - Agent states for request agents  \\n  - Pending questions for request agents\\n  - Request entry from `requests` tracking\\n\\n#### R2: Request-Based Filtering\\n- `get_agent_hierarchy(request_id)` must properly filter by request_id when provided\\n- All methods accepting request_id must filter correctly\\n- Request_id must be properly tracked in all data structures\\n\\n#### R3: Automatic Cleanup\\n- Completed requests older than configurable retention period (default 24 hours) are auto-cleaned\\n- Failed requests older than retention period are auto-cleaned\\n- Running requests are never auto-cleaned\\n- Old activities beyond max_activities limit (default 10,000) are trimmed\\n\\n#### R4: Data Integrity\\n- No data loss for active requests\\n- No data loss for requests within retention period\\n- Cleanup operations are atomic (all-or-nothing)\\n- Parent-child agent relationships maintained during partial cleanup\\n\\n#### R5: Thread Safety\\n- Cleanup operations use proper locking mechanisms\\n- No race conditions with concurrent activity recording\\n- Safe to call cleanup from multiple threads\\n\\n#### R6: Configurability\\n- Retention period configurable (default 24 hours)\\n- Max activities limit configurable (default 10,000)\\n- Cleanup can be triggered manually or automatically\\n- Automatic cleanup interval configurable (default every hour)\\n\\n### Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n#### Performance\\n- Cleanup operations complete within 1 second for typical data volumes\\n- Memory usage remains stable over 24+ hour sessions\\n- No performance impact on activity recording during cleanup\\n\\n#### Reliability\\n- Cleanup failures are logged but don\'t crash the system\\n- Partial cleanup is handled gracefully\\n- System recovers from cleanup errors automatically\\n\\n#### Monitoring\\n- Cleanup operations are logged with details (items removed, time taken)\\n- Memory usage metrics available for monitoring\\n- Cleanup statistics available via API\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n### AC1: clear_request() Implementation\\n- [x] Method removes all activities for the request_id\\n- [x] Method removes all agent hierarchy entries for request agents\\n- [x] Method removes all agent states for request agents\\n- [x] Method removes all pending questions for request agents\\n- [x] Method removes request from requests tracking\\n- [x] Method is thread-safe with proper locking\\n- [x] Method logs cleanup details\\n\\n### AC2: Request Filtering\\n- [x] get_agent_hierarchy(request_id) returns only agents for that request\\n- [x] get_activities(request_id=X) returns only activities for request X\\n- [x] All request-based filtering works correctly\\n\\n### AC3: Automatic Cleanup\\n- [x] Old completed requests are automatically cleaned after retention period\\n- [x] Running requests are never auto-cleaned regardless of age\\n- [x] Activity list is trimmed to max_activities limit\\n- [x] Cleanup runs automatically at configured intervals\\n\\n### AC4: Data Safety\\n- [x] No active request data is lost\\n- [x] Recent request data within retention period is preserved  \\n- [x] Parent-child relationships are maintained correctly\\n- [x] Cleanup is atomic (doesn\'t leave partial state)\\n\\n### AC5: Configuration\\n- [x] Retention period is configurable\\n- [x] Max activities limit is configurable\\n- [x] Automatic cleanup can be enabled/disabled\\n- [x] Manual cleanup can be triggered\\n\\n### AC6: Memory Stability\\n- [x] Memory usage remains stable during 8+ hour test sessions\\n- [x] No memory leaks from incomplete cleanup\\n- [x] System handles cleanup of large request datasets (1000+ activities)\\n\\n## Files to Modify\\n\\n### Primary Implementation\\n- `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py` - Complete cleanup implementation\\n\\n### Test Files (to be created)\\n- `tests/test_activity_tracker_cleanup.py` - Comprehensive cleanup tests\\n\\n## Test Requirements\\n\\n### Test Cases Required\\n\\n#### Unit Tests\\n1. **clear_request() functionality**\\n   - Removes all data for single request\\n   - Handles non-existent request gracefully  \\n   - Thread safety with concurrent operations\\n   - Partial cleanup scenarios\\n\\n2. **Request filtering**\\n   - get_agent_hierarchy filters correctly\\n   - get_activities filters correctly\\n   - Edge cases (empty request, no matches)\\n\\n3. **Automatic cleanup**\\n   - Old requests are cleaned\\n   - Running requests are preserved\\n   - Activity trimming works correctly\\n   - Configuration changes take effect\\n\\n#### Integration Tests\\n1. **Memory stability**\\n   - Long-running session memory usage\\n   - Large dataset cleanup performance\\n   - Concurrent request processing\\n\\n2. **Data integrity**  \\n   - No data loss during cleanup\\n   - Hierarchy relationships preserved\\n   - State consistency after cleanup\\n\\n## TDD Approach\\n1. Write failing tests first for each requirement\\n2. Implement minimum code to pass tests\\n3. Refactor while keeping tests passing\\n4. Add edge case tests and handle them\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n- All tests pass\\n- Memory usage remains stable over long sessions\\n- Cleanup operations complete quickly\\n- No data loss for active requests\\n- Existing functionality unaffected\\n- Code is well-documented and maintainable\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n- Extensive testing with various data scenarios\\n- Gradual rollout with monitoring\\n- Backup/restore capability for critical data\\n- Feature flags for rollback if issues arise\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Current ActivityTracker API remains stable\\n- Thread safety is required for production use\\n- JSON serialization format doesn\'t change\\n- Persistence to disk continues to be supported"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', '