ype': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01JByErRmNvyzygVN6GxosC5', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Request Cleanup System Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## 1. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### System Goal\\nImplement a robust, performant, and configurable request cleanup mechanism for the ActivityTracker to manage memory usage and ensure data integrity during long-running sessions.\\n\\n### Architecture Pattern\\n- **Layered Architecture** with clear separation of concerns\\n- **Strategy Pattern** for configurable cleanup policies\\n- **Thread-safe design** with concurrent access considerations\\n\\n## 2. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Language and Runtime\\n- **Python 3.9+**: Leveraging modern language features\\n- **Threading**: `threading` module for concurrency\\n- **Logging**: `logging` module for comprehensive tracking\\n\\n### Core Libraries\\n- `typing`: Type hinting for robust type management\\n- `dataclasses`: For clean, immutable configuration objects\\n- `concurrent.futures`: For potential future parallel processing\\n\\n## 3. System Components\\n\\n### Core Components\\n1. **CleanupManager**\\n   - Central orchestration of cleanup operations\\n   - Manages retention policies\\n   - Triggers automatic and manual cleanups\\n   - Thread-safe implementation\\n\\n2. **RequestFilter**\\n   - Handles request-based filtering\\n   - Implements efficient filtering algorithms\\n   - Supports complex multi-criteria filtering\\n\\n3. **CleanupStrategy**\\n   - Configurable cleanup policy interface\\n   - Default implementations for time-based and activity-count-based cleanup\\n   - Easily extensible for future policy types\\n\\n### Data Structures\\n- **RetentionPolicy**: Configuration for cleanup rules\\n- **CleanupMetadata**: Tracks cleanup operations metadata\\n- **ThreadSafeContainer**: Custom thread-safe data structure for activities\\n\\n## 4. Detailed Design\\n\\n### Cleanup Implementation Workflow\\n```python\\nclass CleanupManager:\\n    def clear_request(self, request_id: str):\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        Atomically remove all data associated with a request\\n        - Remove activities\\n        - Remove agent hierarchy\\n        - Remove agent states\\n        - Remove pending questions\\n        - Thread-safe with fine-grained locking\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        \\n    def auto_cleanup(self, retention_hours: int = 24, max_activities: int = 10000):\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        Automatic cleanup mechanism\\n        - Remove old completed/failed requests\\n        - Trim activity list\\n        - Configurable retention period\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n\\nclass RequestFilter:\\n    def get_agent_hierarchy(self, request_id: Optional[str] = None):\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n        Filter agent hierarchy by request_id\\n        - Supports filtering\\n        - Handles edge cases (no match, empty request)\\n        \\"\\"\\"\\n```\\n\\n## 5. Configuration Strategy\\n\\n### Configurability Layers\\n- **Default Configuration**\\n  - 24-hour retention\\n  - 10,000 max activities\\n- **Dynamic Configuration**\\n  - Runtime configuration changes\\n  - Configuration file support\\n  - Environment variable overrides\\n\\n## 6. Thread Safety Mechanisms\\n\\n### Synchronization Approach\\n- **Fine-grained locking**\\n  - `threading.Lock()` for critical sections\\n  - `RLock` for reentrant locks\\n- **Atomic operations**\\n- **Lock-free data structures** where possible\\n\\n## 7. Performance Considerations\\n\\n### Optimization Strategies\\n- Minimize lock contention\\n- Use efficient data structures\\n- Lazy deletion and cleanup\\n- Background thread for auto-cleanup\\n\\n## 8. Error Handling & Resilience\\n\\n### Error Management\\n- Comprehensive logging\\n- Graceful degradation\\n- No-crash error handling\\n- Detailed error reporting\\n\\n## 9. Monitoring & Observability\\n\\n### Tracking Mechanisms\\n- Detailed cleanup logs\\n- Performance metrics\\n- Memory usage tracking\\n- Cleanup operation statistics\\n\\n## 10. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Test Coverage\\n- Unit tests for each component\\n- Integration tests for cleanup workflows\\n- Concurrency stress tests\\n- Long-running session simulations\\n\\n## 11. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Potential Risks\\n1. **Performance Overhead**\\n   - Mitigation: Lazy cleanup, background processing\\n2. **Data Loss**\\n   - Mitigation: Atomic operations, extensive validation\\n3. **Concurrency Issues**\\n   - Mitigation: Fine-grained locking, thread-safe design\\n\\n## 12. Future Extensibility\\n\\n### Potential Enhancements\\n- Pluggable cleanup strategies\\n- More granular filtering\\n- Advanced retention policies\\n- Distributed cleanup for large datasets\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture provides a comprehensive, flexible solution for request cleanup, addressing all specified requirements with a focus on performance, safety, and maintainability."}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task 