minate Button**: Add \\"Terminate\\" button to agent cards in UI\\n- **Bulk Actions**: Allow selection and termination of multiple agents\\n- **Confirmation Dialog**: Require confirmation before termination\\n- **Status Indication**: Clear visual indication of which agents can be terminated\\n\\n### 2. Backend Cleanup API\\n- **Terminate Endpoint**: `/api/agents/{agent_id}/terminate` endpoint\\n- **Bulk Terminate**: `/api/agents/terminate-batch` for multiple agents\\n- **State Cleanup**: Remove agent from active agents dictionary\\n- **Database Cleanup**: Mark agent as manually terminated in tracking systems\\n\\n### 3. Safety Mechanisms\\n- **Active Agent Protection**: Prevent termination of currently executing agents\\n- **User Confirmation**: Double-confirmation for bulk operations\\n- **Audit Trail**: Log all manual terminations for accountability\\n- **Undo Protection**: Clear indication that termination is final\\n\\n## User Stories\\n\\n### Primary Users: System Administrators, Power Users\\n\\n**As a user, I want to:**\\n1. See which agents are stalled/inactive in the UI\\n2. Click a button to terminate unwanted agents\\n3. Select multiple agents and terminate them at once\\n4. Be warned before terminating agents that might still be useful\\n5. See immediate confirmation that agents have been cleaned up\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Frontend Updates\\n- Add termination controls to agent monitoring UI\\n- Implement agent selection checkboxes\\n- Add confirmation modals\\n- Update agent status displays after termination\\n\\n### Backend Updates  \\n- Implement agent termination endpoints\\n- Clean up orchestrator state\\n- Update activity tracking systems\\n- Add termination logging\\n\\n### Safety Requirements\\n- Only allow termination of agents in specific states (completed, error, awaiting_input, stalled)\\n- Require explicit user confirmation\\n- Maintain audit trail of all terminations\\n- Graceful handling of already-terminated agents\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **Usability**: Users can terminate agents in 2 clicks (select + confirm)\\n2. **Safety**: No accidental termination of active agents\\n3. **Performance**: UI updates immediately after termination\\n4. **Reliability**: System remains stable after agent cleanup\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Automatic agent cleanup policies\\n- Agent recovery/restart functionality (already exists)\\n- Historical agent data deletion\\n- Real-time agent health monitoring (already exists)\\n\\n## Implementation Assumptions\\n- Users understand that termination is permanent for that agent instance\\n- Existing recovery and monitoring systems will remain unchanged\\n- Agent termination is for cleanup purposes, not debugging\\n- UI will use existing agent state management patterns\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n- **Accidental Termination**: Multi-step confirmation process\\n- **System Instability**: Graceful state cleanup without affecting other agents\\n- **Data Loss**: Clear communication that termination removes agent from active tracking only\\n- **User Confusion**: Clear labeling and help text throughout interface"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION 